---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { ovdbServer, storageEngineCount, storageEntryCount, storageGroups, publicOvdbApiCount } from '../../data/ovdb';
---

<SiteLayout title="OpenVaultDB server · DemoDB" description={ovdbServer.description} canonical="/ovdb/">
  <section class="shell page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Shared read-only data service</p>
    <h1>{ovdbServer.title}</h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">{ovdbServer.description}</p>
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/ovdb/ovdb-server.json">Server descriptor <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-quiet" href={ovdbServer.apiUrl}>API root</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell section">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Storage catalogue</p><h2>{storageGroups.length} datasets. {storageEngineCount} storage engines each.</h2></div><span class="muted">{publicOvdbApiCount} public OVDB APIs · {storageEntryCount} storage entries</span></div>
    <p class="storage-intro">The shared server descriptor lists the six SQLite databases with working public APIs. PostgreSQL copies are hosted on Neon; public OVDB access is pending. inGitDB editions are published in each dataset’s GitHub repository.</p>
    <div class="database-grid">
      {storageGroups.map(({ database, storages }) => (
        <article class="database-card storage-group">
          <span class="database-kicker">{database.recordsets.length} published SQLite collections</span>
          <h2>{database.title}</h2><p>Explore the {database.title} dataset across three storage editions.</p>
          <div class="storage-choices">{storages.map((storage) => <a href={`/ovdb/db/${storage.id}/`}><strong>{storage.engine}<small>{storage.id}</small></strong><span>{storage.readiness === 'public-api' ? 'Public read-only API' : storage.readiness === 'hosted-repository' ? 'Published on GitHub · query locally' : 'Hosted on Neon · public API pending'}<span class="storage-tags">{storage.tags.map((tag) => <span class="storage-tag">{tag}</span>)}</span></span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>)}</div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell section catalogue-note"><p class="eyebrow">Public interface</p><h2>Read and query. Never write.</h2><p>The six SQLite APIs use the shared backend and provider-declared capabilities. Their database manifests expose native table names, columns, keys, provenance, and public semantic references.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/ovdb/schemas/ovdb-server-draft-1.schema.json">Server JSON Schema</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/ovdb/schemas/ovdb-database-draft-1.schema.json">Database JSON Schema</a></p></section>
</SiteLayout>
